From c0ce6d32f92d3035a5e0bed5c563838694823bfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Harris <mharris@vultr.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 22:04:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] fix(rocm): make DeepSeek-V4-Flash load on gfx94*

Six gfx94*-only crashes during DSV4-FP4 boot that MI35x (gfx950)
silently skips, which is why the canonical SGLang DSV4 FP4 test
(test/registered/amd/test_deepseek_v4_flash_fp4.py, mi35x suite)
never tripped them.

Weight load + KV pool init:

1. Fp8MoEMethod.process_weights_after_loading_block_quant
   unconditionally calls normalize_e4m3fn_to_e4m3fnuz on
   layer.w13_weight when _is_fp8_fnuz=True. For
   SGLANG_DSV4_FP4_EXPERTS=true, create_weights allocates these
   tensors as torch.int8 (FP4-packed), so the normalize asserts
   dtype == float8_e4m3fn and crashes. Early-return when
   is_fp4_expert.

2. KVCache.__init__ only switches to uint8-backed storage for
   float8_e5m2 and float8_e4m3fn. DeepSeekV4SingleKVPool packs
   nope_FP8 + rope_BF16 + scales + pad into a raw byte buffer
   and asserts store_dtype == torch.uint8 in create_buffer. The
   gfx94* path normalizes kv_cache_dtype=fp8_e4m3 to
   float8_e4m3fnuz, which then bypassed the uint8 store. Treat
   fnuz the same way.

First forward pass JIT compile of the BF16 Q-norm-rope kernel:

3. deepseek_v4/fp8_utils.cuh unconditionally includes
   <cuda_fp8.h>; missing on ROCm. Gate behind USE_ROCM.

4. Same header's pack_fp8 brace-inits fp8x2_e4m3_t (== uint16_t
   on ROCm) from fp32x2_t, which doesn't parse. The Q-norm-rope
   TU never calls pack_fp8 (only the K and indexer kernels do)
   but the function body is typechecked at definition site.
   Switch to a USE_ROCM branch in the body that __builtin_traps;
   this keeps the symbol around for the using-declarations in
   main_norm_rope.cuh, lets the BF16 Q TU parse, and surfaces a
   clear runtime trap if a future ROCm JIT TU actually invokes
   pack_fp8 without a real HIP packing impl.

5. tensor.h's _dtype_trait specializations for fp16_t/bf16_t/
   fp8_e4m3_t are gated behind __CUDACC__. On hipcc that macro
   isn't defined, so __hip_bfloat16 falls back to no trait at
   all (the std::floating_point generic doesn't match) and
   kDTypeList<__hip_bfloat16> fails to compile. Add ROCm
   specializations for fp16_t/bf16_t with the canonical
   DLDataTypeCode entries; fp8_e4m3_t (== uint8_t on ROCm) is
   already covered by the std::integral generic.

6. warp.cuh's __shfl_xor_sync calls pass a uint32_t active_mask
   but HIP requires uint64_t (gfx9 wavefronts are 64-wide).
   Widen via a SGL_SHFL_MASK macro that no-ops on CUDA.

All six are needed to land a working V4-Flash image on MI300X.

Adapted from local MI300X debugging; not upstreamed.
